course: dictionary
lesson: 57
title: Accustom and accustomed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To accustom yourself to something means to get used to it. «It took a week to accustom myself to the new school.» The clue is «took a week»: getting used to something new takes time, so accustom means becoming familiar with it.
explain: Accustomed is an adjective that means used to something. «I'm accustomed to early mornings.» The speaker is used to getting up early, so it is no surprise to them. Notice that accustomed is followed by to.
explain: Accustomed can also mean usual, especially in formal writing. «She sat in her accustomed seat.» The clue is the word her: she sat in the seat she always uses. Ask yourself, what word would fit here? Usual fits, so accustomed means usual in this sentence.
fact: Accustom is a verb: accustom, accustoms, accustomed, accustoming.
fact: «Accustom yourself to» means to get used to something new.
fact: «Accustomed to» means used to, as in «accustomed to early mornings».
fact: «Accustomed» can also mean usual, as in «her accustomed seat».
fact: In science, eyes become accustomed to the dark: they adjust slowly so you can see more.
exercise: «It took a week to accustom myself to the new school.» What does accustom yourself mean here? | To feel sad about something | To break something | To leave something behind | *To get used to something
exercise: «I'm accustomed to early mornings.» What does accustomed to mean? | *Used to | Tired of, like a boring job | Forgetful of | Afraid of
exercise: «She sat in her accustomed seat.» What does accustomed mean here? | Expensive | Broken | Empty | *Usual
test: «The Mole's cap was missing from its accustomed peg.» What does accustomed mean in this sentence? | Lost forever | Dusty | Painted green | *Usual
test: Which phrase means to get used to something new? | forget all about | wake up early | throw away | *accustom yourself to
exam: Why do eyes become accustomed to the dark? | So they stop working | So they can shut tight and sleep | So they can glow like a lamp | *So they adjust and you can see more
